{"term":"monopoly","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b866abb64b2b5b016b","definition":"A situation, by legal privilege or other agreement, in which solely one party (company, cartel etc.) exclusively provides a particular product or service, dominating that market and generally exerting powerful control over it.","example":"The sale of the leaves and roots was a Government monopoly, and from it the Kings of Kôr derived a large proportion of their private revenue.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["monopsony","polypoly"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antimonopoly","monopolistic","monopolistically","monopolize","monopolization","monopolizer","monopolylike","natural monopoly","pigopoly","premonopoly","promonopoly","semimonopoly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:98f5bea125f7ef81de","definition":"An exclusive control over the trade or production of a commodity or service through exclusive possession.","example":"A land monopoly renders its holder(s) nearly almighty in an agricultural society.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antimonopoly","monopolistic","monopolistically","monopolize","monopolization","monopolizer","monopolylike","natural monopoly","pigopoly","premonopoly","promonopoly","semimonopoly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ef84a21358a307167a","definition":"The privilege granting the exclusive right to exert such control.","example":"Granting monopolies in concession constitutes a market-conform alternative to taxation for the state, while the crown sometimes bestowed a monopoly as an outrageous gift.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antimonopoly","monopolistic","monopolistically","monopolize","monopolization","monopolizer","monopolylike","natural monopoly","pigopoly","premonopoly","promonopoly","semimonopoly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7d4fa89d84f39287cc","definition":"The market thus controlled.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"metonymically","register":"metonymically","wordFamily":["antimonopoly","monopolistic","monopolistically","monopolize","monopolization","monopolizer","monopolylike","natural monopoly","pigopoly","premonopoly","promonopoly","semimonopoly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3d73bc05fc50299772","definition":"The holder (person, company or other) of such market domination in one of the above manners.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["monopolist"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"metonymically","register":"metonymically","wordFamily":["antimonopoly","monopolistic","monopolistically","monopolize","monopolization","monopolizer","monopolylike","natural monopoly","pigopoly","premonopoly","promonopoly","semimonopoly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3d55c3712f82190abb","definition":"A board game in which players use play money to buy and trade properties, with the objective of forcing opponents into bankruptcy.","example":"I was playing Monopoly with my friends at 12:00am last night.","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antim